-foot><fn><p>Scoring system (1-5) is the same as tests of the upper extremity (mimimum 10, maximum 50).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Criteria for impairment of upper extremities in brain injured persons</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-S247-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>, Optional test.</p><p>ROM, range of motion.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Criteria for rating impairments of upper extremities relating to central impairment</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-S247-i004"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Criteria for impairment of lower extremities in brain injured persons</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-S247-i005"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>, Optional test.</p><p>ROM, range of motion.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T6" position="float"><label>Table 6</label><caption><p>Criteria for rating impairments of lower extremities relating to central impairment</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-S247-i006"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>AMA, American Medical Association.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>